{"id":"kd25ec669a2e22749","type":"law","name":"cascade_noise_margin","informal":"In a cascade, the upstream gate's OFF level must sit below the downstream gate's half-maximal input and its ON level above it. Otherwise the downstream gate cannot tell the two states apart and the circuit's logic is not realised in the cell.","lean_file":"tracks/kernel/lean/CircuitLaws.lean","lean_sha":"8c37443974971f00","lean_decls":["Delphi.Circuit.margins_pos","Delphi.Circuit.no_margin_of_le"],"script":null,"audit":{"tool":"tracks/lean/check.sh","toolchain":"leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0","verdict":"CHECKED","detail":null,"axioms":["Classical.choice","Quot.sound","propext"],"axioms_are":"the bound check.sh confirmed every audited theorem was within","audited":6,"at":"2026-11-19T06:12:25.066Z"},"prev":"k1b1dedb29b4c76fb","kernel":"0.1.0"}
{"id":"k5aad595156abd993","type":"law","name":"distinct_orthogonal_repressors","informal":"Two gates in one circuit must use repressors that do not bind each other's promoters. A repressor used twice, or a pair the record reports as cross-reacting, makes the wiring diagram and the cell disagree.","lean_sha":null,"lean_decls":[],"script":"tracks/kernel/compile/compile.mjs (orthogonality check over the crosstalk groups in parts.json)","audit":null,"prev":"kd25ec669a2e22749","kernel":"0.1.0"}
{"id":"k5c42ac13833aed1f","type":"law","name":"model_parameters_present","informal":"A predictive model of a gate needs four numbers: both output levels, the half-maximal input and the cooperativity. A model built with any of them guessed is not a prediction.","lean_sha":null,"lean_decls":[],"script":"tracks/kernel/compile/emit.mjs (parameter completeness per gate)","audit":null,"prev":"k5aad595156abd993","kernel":"0.1.0"}
